From 43d23b06382eba7e51269a18e43bd9712346588e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Your Name <gamefroggy16@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:40:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sd-boot: mirror the menu across every display

sd-boot renders only through ST->ConOut, the firmware ConSplitter, which forces
one shared text mode on every console and reaches whichever displays the
firmware happened to wire up. GOP is consulted only to query a resolution, via
LocateProtocol, which returns the first handle.

Drive the displays directly instead. gop.c enumerates every GOP handle and puts
each into its EDID preferred mode (falling back to whatever POST chose -- not
the largest, since firmware maximums are often far above the panel). textfb.c
implements EFI_SIMPLE_TEXT_OUTPUT_PROTOCOL over an embedded 8x16 bitmap font,
upscaled per display so a 1080p TV and a 1440p monitor read alike, and installs
itself as ST->ConOut. Taking the protocol over rather than abstracting the call
sites means util.c, efi-string.c and efi-log.c keep working untouched, and the
menu mirrors to every display at its own native resolution.

The character grid is shared and sized to the smallest display, which is what
makes this a mirror. ST->ConOut is handed back before chainloading, since the
protocol lives in sd-boot own memory.

console_key_read() already waits on a timer, so it now also ticks once a second
to re-assert modes and adopt displays that show up late; a monitor asleep at
POST can be woken this way. multigop-reconnect additionally forces a controller
re-probe, which is disruptive and therefore off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
